  },
  "pages": [
    {
      "name": "intro",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "html",
          "name": "intro_overview",
          "html": "<h3>Purpose</h3><p>This survey asks Wyoming voters what standards should guide large data center development in our state. The goal is to measure public input, not argue for or against any specific project.</p><p><a class=\"button button--small button--secondary\" href=\"/assets/wy_data_centers_sources_background.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Sources and background</a> &nbsp; <a class=\"button button--small button--secondary\" href=\"/assets/wy_data_centers_purpose_privacy.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Privacy and method</a></p><h3>How responses will be used</h3><ul><li>Results will be published in aggregate.</li><li>Exact question wording and response options will be published with the results.</li><li>Verified and unverified responses may be reported separately.</li><li>Individual responses will remain confidential.</li></ul><h3>Short background</h3><p>Wyoming is seeing increased interest in large data centers and other large-load facilities. These projects may bring investment, jobs, and tax revenue. They may also affect water, electric infrastructure, land use, local services, wildlife, housing, and utility costs. This survey asks what conditions Wyoming voters believe should apply before projects move forward.</p><h3>Definitions</h3><ul><li><strong>Data center:</strong> A facility with computer servers used to store, process, or move digital information.</li><li><strong>Large-load facility:</strong> A project requiring a large amount of electricity.</li><li><strong>Closed-loop cooling system:</strong> A system that reuses cooling water rather than relying on continuous new water use.</li></ul>"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "baseline_view",
      "title": "Section 1: Familiarity and overall view",
      "description": "Where you start — your familiarity with the issue and your current overall position.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "radiogroup",
          "name": "data_center_familiarity",
          "title": "How familiar are you with data center development in Wyoming?",
          "choices": [
            "Very familiar",
            "Somewhat familiar",
            "Not very familiar",
            "Not familiar",
            "Not sure"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "radiogroup",
          "name": "overall_view",
          "title": "Which statement is closest to your overall view?",
          "choices": [
            "Wyoming should welcome data centers with ordinary review",
            "Wyoming should welcome data centers only with clear safeguards",
            "Wyoming should pause new large data center approvals until stronger rules are in place",
            "Wyoming should generally discourage large data center development",
            "Not sure"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "benefits_and_concerns",
